# A divisor whose range includes zero though zero is not an instance.
-- source.cue --
d: int & !=0 & >=-5 & <=5
-- target.cue --
q: int
-- lens.cue --
input: _
result: {q: quo(10, input.d)}
-- out --
unknown
result.q divides by input.d, whose range [-5, 5] includes 0, though 0 may not be an instance; bound the divisor away from 0 (>0 or <0) (rule unknown-divisor) @ lens.cue:2:17
